SM wrote:
> Good to know. BTW, I think I encountered a minor bug. When blind (by any
> means, with or without telepathy) and #chat'ing in any direction where
> there are no monsters, message is "You feel no door there". Not sure if
> it should be like that but still.

#chat is bound to "c" by default. When there are no monsters on the
square, it acts like "o" (unlock, open or close door) instead, in order
to not screw up the muscle memory of vanilla players. So it's not
exactly a bug; it's more the interface not having enough information to
know which error message to give.

Perhaps it should assume c = chat if the player isn't aware of a door on
the square, or if it's occupied by a monster the player is aware of, and
= close otherwise.

